    {
      "text": "Let the center be \\((h,0)\\).  \nSince both points lie on the circle, their distances to the center are equal:\n\n\\[\n(h-0)^2 + (0-4)^2 = (h-1)^2 + (0-3)^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\nh^2 + 16 = (h-1)^2 + 9\n\\]\n\n\\[\nh^2 + 16 = h^2 - 2h + 1 + 9\n\\]\n\n\\[\n16 = -2h + 10\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2h = -6\n\\]\n\n\\[\nh = -3\n\\]\n\nThe radius is the distance from \\((-3,0)\\) to \\((0,4)\\):\n\n\\[\nr = \\sqrt{(0+3)^2 + (4-0)^2}\n= \\sqrt{9+16}\n= 5\n\\]\n\nThe answer is 5.",
